Car MPG Predictor
========================================================
author: Your Name
date: `r Sys.Date()`
autosize: true
font-family: 'Georgia'
css: custom.css

A Shiny application for predicting fuel efficiency using the `mtcars` dataset.

---

The Problem
========================================================

**How fuel-efficient is a car with given specs?**

- Fuel efficiency (MPG) matters for **cost, environment, and purchasing decisions**
- It's hard to estimate without running tests — but regression can help!
- The classic `mtcars` dataset (Motor Trend, 1974) gives us a foundation

```{r, echo=FALSE}
data(mtcars)
cat("Dataset: mtcars |", nrow(mtcars), "cars |", ncol(mtcars), "variables\n")
cat("MPG range:", min(mtcars$mpg), "–", max(mtcars$mpg), "| Mean:", round(mean(mtcars$mpg),1))
```

---

The Model
========================================================

A **linear regression** model predicts MPG from 4 key inputs:

| Input | Variable | Range |
|-------|----------|-------|
| Cylinders | `cyl` | 4, 6, 8 |
| Horsepower | `hp` | 50–340 |
| Weight | `wt` | 1.5–5.5 klbs |
| Transmission | `am` | 0=Auto, 1=Manual |

```{r}
model <- lm(mpg ~ cyl + hp + wt + am, data = mtcars)
round(summary(model)$r.squared, 3)   # R-squared
```

**R² = `r round(summary(lm(mpg ~ cyl + hp + wt + am, data=mtcars))$r.squared, 3)`** — the model explains ~87% of MPG variance.

---

The Shiny App
========================================================

**Features at a glance:**

- 🎛️ **Radio buttons** to select cylinder count (4 / 6 / 8)
- 🎚️ **Sliders** for horsepower and weight
- 📋 **Dropdown** for transmission type
- 📊 **Reactive histogram** showing where your car sits vs. all `mtcars` cars
- 📐 **Confidence interval** displayed alongside the point estimate
- 📄 **Model summary** table always visible for transparency

All documentation is embedded directly in the app — no external links needed.

---

Live Demo & Links
========================================================

```{r, echo=FALSE, fig.width=7, fig.height=4}
model <- lm(mpg ~ cyl + hp + wt + am, data = mtcars)
pred_example <- predict(model,
  newdata = data.frame(cyl=4, hp=110, wt=2.6, am=1))

hist(mtcars$mpg, col="#AED6F1", border="white",
     main="MPG Distribution + Example Prediction",
     xlab="Miles Per Gallon", ylab="Count")
abline(v=pred_example, col="#e74c3c", lwd=3, lty=2)
legend("topright",
       legend=paste("4-cyl, 110hp, 2.6klb, manual →", round(pred_example,1), "MPG"),
       col="#e74c3c", lwd=2, lty=2, bty="n")
```

